;; The module _weakref (PY5e; Modules/_weakref.c, Objects/weakrefobject.c): ref (ReferenceType), proxy (ProxyType,
;; CallableProxyType) and their helpers. Since queue 218 a weak reference does not hold its referent (finalize.go,
;; PYS9 (a)): the referent is tracked, its address hidden from Go's collector, and when the collector finds it
;; unreachable its weak references are cleared and their callbacks called, newest first after the basic ref and proxy
;; (CPython's list), the basic ref and proxy (no callback) reused. A referent finalize.go cannot track (another
;; package's object, which may carry its own Go finalizer) is held, as before 218: its references never die.

